# config/axes/Kconfig.preset — PRESET, the one choice a defconfig needs
#
# Seven axes describe what an image is:
#   HWCLASS    the hardware class            (config/axes/Kconfig.hwclass)
#   USE        what the image is for         (config/axes/Kconfig.use, USE_*; derived 1:1 from the
#                                             preset, not a choice)
#   STRUCTURE  where the drivers run         (config/axes/Kconfig.structure)
#   RT         the real-time class           (config/axes/Kconfig.rt)
#   SECURITY   the security posture          (config/axes/Kconfig.security)
#   BUILD_TYPE dev / release / certifiable   (config/axes/Kconfig.build)
#   VIRT       the hypervisor role           (config/axes/Kconfig.virt)
# and one choice, PRESET, sets all of them at once. A defconfig is one PRESET
# line plus its board lines (ISA, board, RAM, the HWCLASS the board is).
#
# A preset works only through `default ... if PRESET_*` on the axes and
# through the axes' own `default`/`imply` lines on the options they own; it
# never `select`s. Every axis can be changed by hand after the preset, and a
# value set by hand wins. A hard incompatibility is a `depends on`.
#
# USE is what was called the application domain: it has no menu of its own and is
# set by the PRESET alone (a defconfig names the preset, never a USE_* symbol).
# Its symbols are USE_* (the cargo feature `use-robot`, the generated
# constants and the robot menus are named after it). "Domain" now names only the isolation object.

choice
    prompt "Preset"
    default PRESET_GENERIC
    help
      One choice that sets every axis below (and, through them, the options
      the axes own) to the values the preset needs. Choose the closest
      preset first, then change an axis or an option by hand where the
      product differs: a value set by hand wins over the preset's. The
      board lines of a defconfig (ISA, board, RAM size, HWCLASS) are not
      the preset's: a robot on a 64 MiB board is PRESET_ROBOT with
      HWCLASS_EMBEDDED.

      The presets do not set BUILD_TYPE: a QEMU image is a development
      build and a board image a release build whatever the preset is.
      `make check-presets` expands every preset on every ISA.

    config PRESET_GENERIC
        bool "General: Generic (QEMU, development, evaluation)"
        help
          A general-purpose kernel: USE generic, RT none, hybrid structure,
          general security. The old edge/embedded/fleet defconfigs.

    config PRESET_ROBOT
        bool "Embedded control: Robot (mobile robots, drones, robotic arms)"
        depends on CAP_SLOT_EXT
        help
          USE robot (the robot crates and tasks are linked), RT hard. The
          durable refusal receipt (DECISION_REFUSALS_DURABLE) is on in
          every preset. Write-ahead receipts for ring-3 motor ops
          (EFFECT_WRITE_AHEAD) are on in this preset, because USE is robot;
          no other preset links the robot crates.
          Needs CAP_SLOT_EXT: the behavior loop reaches the ring-3 inference
          service through a badged endpoint capability, which a one-word
          capability slot cannot hold, so without it every cycle would end
          unavailable and the loop would stay at STOP for good.

    config PRESET_INDUSTRIAL
        bool "Embedded control: Industrial (PLC, CNC, motion control)"
        help
          USE industrial, RT hard, SECURITY separation-static, VIRT static,
          memory committed at map time (no demand paging).

    config PRESET_AUTOMOTIVE
        bool "Embedded control: Automotive (ECU, ADAS, telematics)"
        help
          As industrial, USE automotive.

    config PRESET_FIRMWARE
        bool "Embedded control: Firmware (BMC, storage or power controllers)"
        help
          USE firmware on HWCLASS embedded, RT soft, hardened.

    config PRESET_IOT_HMI
        bool "Connected devices: IoT / HMI (smart panels, kiosks, appliances)"
        help
          USE iot-hmi (display, touch, battery), RT soft, hardened.

    config PRESET_WEARABLE
        bool "Connected devices: Wearable (smartwatch, fitness band)"
        help
          USE wearable on HWCLASS embedded, RT soft, hardened.

    config PRESET_GATEWAY
        bool "Connected devices: Gateway (edge router, protocol bridge)"
        help
          USE gateway (the larger network tables), RT soft, hardened.

    config PRESET_DESKTOP
        bool "Computers: Desktop (workstation, laptop, mini-PC)"
        help
          USE desktop on HWCLASS desktop, RT soft, hardened, demand paging;
          VIRT hosted on x86_64 and split on aarch64.

    config PRESET_SERVER
        bool "Computers: Server (rack server, cloud node, NAS)"
        help
          USE server on HWCLASS server (the Fleet cap tables), RT none,
          hardened; VIRT hosted on x86_64 and split on aarch64.

endchoice
